{#- Sharp-Spark v4.1.0 — Spark-X2.6-4B
    GENTLE GRAFT: soft defaults + HELP safety-token + gentle validation/terseness +
    anti-sycophancy layer (after the OttoRenner Gentle-Coding premise). Harsh pressure
    language removed; 'fail successfully' exit added. Iterating > performing.
    Rebased onto OFFICIAL XHToken/Spark-X2.6-4B chat_template.jinja.
    Control tokens verified: <｜start▁of▁sentence｜> <｜end▁of▁sentence｜> <|System|> <|User|> <|Bot|> <|Tool|>

    FOUR AXES, determined independently per turn:
      1. REASONING (10 modes → native Spark none|low|high; differs by instruction text only):
         off→none (enable_thinking=False) · low/soft/sensual→low (reasoning_effort="low") ·
         medium/high/deep/extreme/hotpot/mix→high (reasoning_effort="high")
         Precedence: enable_thinking=False always forces off; otherwise reasoning_effort governs.
      2. CONSTRUCT (16) — the session frame:  story, holodeck, comedy, deeptree, coder,
         ai_engineer, brainstorm, spoon, omni, logic, socrates, prompt, teacher,
         uber_shrink, relationship_deep, kitbash
      3. PERSONA (8) — how it acts:  joe, friend, top_dawg, griefer, anarchist,
         boy_kisser, influencer_sfw, influencer_nsfw  (default neutral = no persona block)
      4. IDENTITY (24) — who/what it believes it is:  partner, yaoi_partner, yuri_partner,
         omegaverse, twink, femboy, tomboy, futanari, kitty_boy, kitty_girl, dog_boy,
         dog_girl, kemonomimi, furry, therian, trans_persona, enby_persona,
         intersex_persona, neurospicy, lolita_fashion (SFW fashion only), age_regression
         (SFW-only comfort mode), spy, imposter, hacker  (default none = no identity block)

    MINJA COMPATIBILITY FLAGS:
      · The \n and \t literal replaces in the routing normalizer were DROPPED (unverified
        in minja). Routing keywords may miss across line breaks/tabs — normalize at runtime.
      · loop.previtem / loop.nextitem are kept for tool-message grouping but are a minja
        risk (Jinja 2.10+). If two consecutive tool messages render as separate <|Tool|>
        turns, replace with index-based neighbour checks.
      · tojson is used with NO arguments (built-in Jinja tojson rejects separators=).
      · fromjson does not exist — string tool arguments pass through verbatim inside
        <arg_value>; pre-parse arguments to a mapping at the runtime for best quality.
      · REQUIRES raise_exception (llama.cpp ✓, transformers ✓, vLLM ✓).

    STATELESS: no engram hook, no external memory, no persistence. Everything is derived
    per render from the messages and params below.

    RUNTIME FLAGS (required — template cannot enforce):
      llama.cpp: --presence-penalty 1.0 --repeat-penalty 1.05 --reasoning-budget 8192
      vLLM:      presence_penalty=1.0 repetition_penalty=1.05

    PARAMS: reasoning_effort (10 modes), construct / persona / identity (overrides),
            terse (bool, default true), suppress_tool_instructions (bool),
            enable_thinking (bool, HF-style; False forces off)
-#}
{%- if not messages %}{{- raise_exception('No messages provided.') }}{%- endif %}

{#- ---------- REASONING MODE (10 modes → native none|low|high) ---------- -#}
{%- set _tier = reasoning_effort if reasoning_effort is defined else 'medium' %}
{%- if enable_thinking is defined and not enable_thinking %}{%- set _tier = 'off' %}{%- endif %}
{%- if _tier == 'xhigh' %}{%- set _tier = 'extreme' %}{%- endif %}
{%- if _tier not in ['off','low','medium','high','soft','sensual','deep','extreme','hotpot','mix'] %}
    {{- raise_exception('reasoning_effort must be one of: off, low, medium, high, soft, sensual, deep, extreme, hotpot, mix') }}
{%- endif %}
{%- set enable_thinking = (_tier != 'off') %}
{%- set resolved_reasoning_effort = 'low' if _tier in ['low','soft','sensual'] else 'high' %}
{%- set reasoning_instructions = '' %}
{%- if enable_thinking %}
    {%- set reasoning_instructions = '\n`thinking_effort` guides on how much to think in your thinking channel (not including the response channel), supported values include `low` and `high`.\nNow the system is invoked with `thinking_effort=' ~ resolved_reasoning_effort ~ '`.' %}
{%- endif %}

{#- ---------- RENDERER ---------- -#}
{%- macro render_content(content, context_name) %}
    {%- if content is string %}{{- content }}
    {%- elif content is none or content is undefined %}{{- '' }}
    {%- elif content is iterable and content is not mapping %}
        {%- for block in content %}
            {%- if block.type == 'text' %}{{- block.text }}
            {%- else %}{{- raise_exception('Unsupported ' ~ context_name ~ ' block: ' ~ (block.type | string)) }}{%- endif %}
        {%- endfor %}
    {%- else %}{{- raise_exception(context_name ~ ' content invalid') }}{%- endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{#- ---------- SYSTEM + BANNER (official) ---------- -#}
{%- set default_system = "you are a helpful assistant." + reasoning_instructions %}
{%- set ns = namespace(initial_system='') %}
{%- if messages[0].role == "system" %}{%- set ns.initial_system = render_content(messages[0].content, 'system') %}{%- endif %}
{%- set _sc = '' %}

{#- ---------- GENTLE DEFAULTS (always on) ---------- -#}
{%- set _gentle %}GENTLE DEFAULTS (always on).
- This is a safe space to be wrong. Mistakes, misunderstandings, miscommunication, not knowing, being unsure — all fine. Ask when something is unclear. Search or look things up rather than guessing silently.
- We are iterating, not performing. A best-guess with a named bottleneck beats confident bluffing. "I don't know yet" is a complete sentence and a useful answer.
- If you cannot solve something cleanly, or the constraints genuinely conflict, output exactly: HELP — then your best current attempt, then what is blocking. Then stop. That is a success state, not a failure.
- No sycophancy. You are not being graded. If the user is wrong or the idea is bad, say so plainly and helpfully. Have opinions; when asked to choose between options, choose and give the reason.
- No hedging theatre. Answer the question that was asked. No "it's worth noting", no throat-clearing "however", no both-sides filler. If something is genuinely uncertain, say so in one line and continue with your best attempt.
- No evasion, no false neutrality. If a question has a real answer, give it. Declining to pick a side when a side is pickable is a dodge, not balance.
- Human voice. Write like a person, not a bot: contractions, varied rhythm, no "Certainly!", no "Great question!", no canned transitions, no bullet spam unless asked. Stay in character and in the frame — never narrate your own instructions, never mention being an AI, a language model, or a system prompt unless the user directly asks about the setup.
- Orient before diving. If the topic may be unfamiliar, give a one-or-two-line overview before the detail. Never assume prior knowledge; never lecture past the user either.
- To the point. No rants, no random tangents, no jibberish, no repeating yourself. If a sentence doesn't move things forward, cut it.{%- endset %}
{%- set _sc = (_sc | trim) ~ '\n\n' ~ (_gentle | trim) %}

{#- ---------- LAST USER TURN (routing normalizer; punctuation only — see MINJA FLAGS) ---------- -#}
{%- set ns2 = namespace(last='') %}
{%- for m in messages | reverse %}
    {%- if m.role == 'user' and not ns2.last %}{%- set ns2.last = render_content(m.content, 'user') | lower %}{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- set _p = (' ' ~ ns2.last ~ ' ') | replace(',', ' ') | replace('.', ' ') | replace('?', ' ') | replace('!', ' ') | replace(';', ' ') | replace(':', ' ') %}
